      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 1999 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Coronary rupture is a rare complication of percutaneous coronary intervention. However, it may be associated with serious hemodynamic consequences often leading to tamponade, myocardial infarction, emergency surgical intervention, or death. We report a successful percutaneous repair of a brisk left anterior descending coronary artery perforation by the implantation of a Magic Wallstent."
      },
